# Copy to .env (gitignored) — settings shared by the pipelines.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Per-component settings stay in their own .env: fieldserver/, mobile/, and
# the corpus tooling's. This one is for the things the training pipelines need,
# which are paths to data that lives outside the repo.
#
# Every line here is a *default already in force*. Nothing needs uncommenting to
# work — uncomment a line when your layout differs from the assumption.

# The shared corpus (audio + its DB). Defaults to ./data, which is gitignored.
# Point it at another disk when the recordings outgrow this one.
#DATA_DIR=/home/you/Code/cawtalker/data

# Where `make backup` copies the field recordings and the database.
#
# The audio and the database are the only irreplaceable things here — a lost
# capture does not come back, and the ★ Keep ones are the only real crow audio
# in a corpus otherwise made of seeded clips. data/ is excluded by default
# because the corpus tooling can supply it again.
#
# An external drive is the point. A backup on the same disk survives a mistake
# but not a disk. `make backup` refuses if this does not already exist, because
# an unmounted drive looks identical to a folder nobody created yet.
#BACKUP_DIR=/media/ben/drive/cawtalker
